+From d8e7ae78c4a2b22139d2f140f7eb36c219ad710b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: "evgenii.zelenkov" <evgenii.zelenkov@gdasuclite.com>
+Date: Mon, 4 May 2026 03:56:07 +0300
+Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat: add vase bottom sealing passes for spiral vase mode
+MIME-Version: 1.0
+Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
+Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
+
+Adds two complementary gap-fill passes for spiral vase bottom layers:
+
+1. Seal bottom large voids (vase_bottom_gap_fill)
+   - medial-axis gap fill targeting voids >= min_area (default 0.20 mm²)
+   - own flow ratio (default 1.15) and layer limit
+
+2. Seal bottom micro voids (vase_bottom_micro_void_seal)
+   - bounding-box stroke pass for sub-medial-axis voids < max_area
+   - own flow ratio (default 1.15) and layer limit
+
+Both passes run only in spiral_mode on solid bottom layers.
+Call order is configurable via "Seal micro voids before large voids" toggle
+so users can choose whether micro-void or large-void pass runs first.
+
+All 9 new options invalidate posInfill in both Print.cpp and PrintObject.cpp
+so the model re-slices reliably on every setting change.
+
+Settings appear in Others → Special Mode (Advanced, spiral_mode required).
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
